Facts and law texts in this repository come from four sources.

Wikidata (https://www.wikidata.org/): CC0 1.0 Universal.

United Nations Treaty Collection (https://treaties.un.org/): the treaty names and the dates of treaty actions are facts. No other text from the UN pages is reproduced. Source credit: United Nations Treaty Collection, status pages of multilateral treaties deposited with the Secretary-General.

FAOLEX, the FAO legal database (https://faolex.fao.org/): the law texts marked "secondary copy (FAOLEX, ...)"
in acts/, orders/, amending-orders/ and subsidiary/ are FAOLEX's copies. FAO terms
(https://www.fao.org/contact-us/terms/): material may be copied, downloaded and printed for private study,
research and teaching purposes, or for use in non-commercial products or services, provided that FAO is
acknowledged as the source. Source credit: FAOLEX, Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations.

WIPO Lex (https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/): the law texts marked "secondary copy (WIPO Lex, ...)" are WIPO Lex's
copies of national laws, provided free of charge by WIPO. Source credit: WIPO Lex, World Intellectual
Property Organization.

The laws themselves are Brunei's. No text is taken from the Attorney General's Chambers site (agc.gov.bn),
whose Terms of Use require written permission to reproduce its material; none of the copies used carries a
notice requiring that permission.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
